        307.94921875,
        300.10333251953125,
        321.2393798828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "particles. A box particle occupies a small and controllable",
      "bbox": [
        48.95994567871094,
        319.8293151855469,
        300.34295654296875,
        333.1194763183594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "rectangular region of non-zero volume in the target state space.",
      "bbox": [
        48.95994567871094,
        331.8293151855469,
        300.090576171875,
        345.1194763183594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A box-particle ﬁlter (Box-PF) has a potential to signiﬁcantly",
      "bbox": [
        48.9599609375,
        343.8293151855469,
        300.1813049316406,
        357.1194763183594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "reduce the number of required particles, without a loss in",
      "bbox": [
        48.95994567871094,
        355.70941162109375,
        300.0612487792969,
        368.99957275390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the error performance. The concept of the Box-PF was ﬁrst",
      "bbox": [
        48.95994567871094,
        367.70941162109375,
        300.0096740722656,
        380.99957275390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "proposed in [14], using the interval analysis framework to",
      "bbox": [
        48.95994567871094,
        379.5895080566406,
        300.0611572265625,
        392.8796691894531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "propagate weighted boxes in a sequential way. Subsequently,",
      "bbox": [
        48.95994567871094,
        391.5895080566406,
        300.33062744140625,
        404.8796691894531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
